 - **City attack oscillation — pre-check vs strong targets (possible mitigation)**: In `CvUnitAI::AI_attackCityMove`, add a sanity check to **skip marching to/attacking a city** when the **defending stack is too strong**. Goal: prevent the inefficient **advance → abort → backtrack** loop and reduce the risk of being caught without time to retreat. **Note:** in the test sample, this behavior also resolved without the change by running ~2+ autoplay turns in a row instead of 1 turn only from a slightly older save file rather; treat this as a **possible fix/sanity check** (not (at least not yet) broadly tested). See [KI#63](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#63---possibly-prevented-and-possibly-fixed-weird--very-inefficient-back-and-forth-of-going-to-attack-a-city-stack-and-then-going-back-after-seeing-enemy-stack-is-too-strong-i-dont-know-if-this-change-fixes-it-since-the-issue-was-solved-without-it-2-autoplay-turns-were-needed-at-least-it-seems-not-1-but-maybe-this-change-in-cvunitaiai_attackcitymove-helps-a-lot-but-anyways-etc).
 - **Early-game razing — distance-aware captures**: Updated conquer/raze logic so that, for roughly the first **~120 turns** (scaled by game speed), the AI **razes captured cities** that aren’t **close enough** to justify early investment. This addresses the base AdvCiv pattern where forces overextend (most troops sit in a faraway capture while **core cities** thin out) and also preserves scarce early economy (city maintenance, low pop, time to build improvements/culture). Indirect effect: less fog-busting far from us → **more barbarians** there, which tends to pressure rivals. Net: a **stronger, more focused** early AI (fewer “split in two” empires). See [KI#64](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#64---greatly-enhanced-ai-not-razing-faraway-cities-at-captures---now-we-raze-them-if-we-are-in-the-early-game-and-they-are-not-close-enough-thanks-to-changes-and-tweaks-in-cvplayeraiai_conquercity-anyways-etc).
 - **Early defender overbuild → switch to versatile offense (AI)**: Heuristic in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` reduces **early-game overproduction of pure defenders** (especially Longbowmen) by swapping the build to a more **offensive/versatile** unit when defense is already sufficient — e.g., Spearmen, Axemen, Camel Archers, or civ-specific UUs like War Chariots. Also caps/avoids siege (esp. Trebuchets) when they’re inefficient defensively; production can drop **down to zero** if conditions warrant. If no good replacement exists, the AI can **reflag** the chosen defender to an **attack/attack_city/counter** `UnitAI` instead. In testing, this produced **fewer pure defenders** and **more varied stacks** (e.g., a run where Hatshepsut shifted from ~30 Longbowmen at T130 to ~32 War Chariots, plus Camel Archers). See [KI#53.2](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#532---fixed-and-enhanced-joao-ai-building-way-too-many-defenders-36-longbowmen-at-turn-130-almost-all-with-unitai_city_defense-or-similar-while-being-boxed-in-with-only-3-cities-instead-of-making-about-half-of-these-offense-units-or-versatile-ones-to-punish-overextending-thin-neighbour-fixed-by-having-an-early-phase-we-have-expectedly-too-few-cities-at-this-stage-of-the-game-no-need-to-overbuild-anymore-denders-at-this-stage-of-the-game-switch-to-offense-or-versatile-unitai-rather-and-our-military-composition-has-way-too-many-defender-unitais-switch-to-offense-or-versatile-unitais-which-seemingly-fix-the-issue-anyways-etc) and [KI#53.2.2](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#5322-seemingly-greatly-enhanced-ai-overproducing-defenders-early-on-especially-longbowmen-but-not-only-replaced-with-an-early-produce-more-versatile-units-especially-civ-specific-ones-when-defended-enough-at-least-in-theory-anyways-etc-in-cvcityaiai_chooseunit-anyways-etc).
-- **Siege production — conditional minimization (trebuchets especially)**: In `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit`, added targeted checks to keep **siege output** as low as needed—**up to none at all** when conditions say they’re poor value (e.g., when the AI is **weaker** or not preparing **city assaults**). Rationale: **trebuchets** are very **hammer-inefficient** outside direct city attacks; **catapults/cannons** also aren’t versatile enough (and are often misused) for defense. Current tuning intentionally leans **low** versus before (but not permanently zero when other conditions are met). Result: **more varied offensive stacks** and **stronger defense** when behind. See [KI#53.3](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#533-tremendously-improved-ai-overbuilding-siege-units-in-particular-trebuchets-but-not-only-where-they-are-detrimental-to-do-build-in-particular-when-weaker-but-not-only-anyways-etc).
+- **Siege production — conditional minimization (trebuchets especially)**: In `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit`, added targeted checks to keep **siege output** as low as needed—**up to none at all** when conditions say they’re poor value (e.g., when the AI is **weaker** or not preparing **city assaults**). Rationale: **trebuchets** are very **hammer-inefficient** outside direct city attacks; **catapults/cannons** also aren’t versatile enough (and are often misused) for defense. Current tuning intentionally leans **low** versus before (but not permanently zero when other conditions are met). Result: **more varied offensive stacks** and **stronger defense** when behind. See [KI#53.3](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#533-tremendously-improved-ai-overbuilding-siege-units-in-particular-trebuchets-but-not-only-where-they-are-detrimental-to-do-build-in-particular-when-weaker-but-not-only-anyways-etc). **Update:** From the **Renaissance** onward, thresholds are **heavily relaxed** in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` and in `CvCity::doTurn`—when **Cannons** unlock they can serve as a practical **defensive pivot** (esp. if you lack bonuses/muskets), and the AI avoids **over-producing Pikemen** into **Cuirassiers**, leading to **more varied stacks** and improved survival. See [KI#53.3](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#533-tremendously-improved-ai-overbuilding-siege-units-in-particular-trebuchets-but-not-only-where-they-are-detrimental-to-do-build-in-particular-when-weaker-but-not-only-anyways-etc).
 - **City-counter role pruning (e.g. Macemen)**: Removed `UNITAI_CITY_COUNTER` from **non-versatile** units (e.g., `UNIT_MACEMAN`). For example for macemen, as city defenders they’re too easy to punish—knights counter them hard, and even crossbow stacks can beat defending macemen—so they’re better assigned to **offensive** `UnitAI` roles. While macemen beat pikemen, pikes seldom assault cities efficiently, so the city-counter slot isn’t warranted. The same adjustment applies to any other units with this mismatch.
 - **Very cheap-combat spam cap (tiered & generalized):** The AI was **overbuilding very cheap combat units**—notably the **Ancient Maceman**—even ~T100. Because they’re so cheap, they pile up, are weak once Archers appear, and can drag the economy. We added conditions in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` to **limit** these builds, with a **stricter cap after ~T50** when they’re especially poor value. In SAS, Archers arrive early, are cheap/versatile, and fill defense quotas sooner, letting cities pivot to offense. (Scouts get trimmed incidentally since they’re combat-tagged, though they weren’t the main issue.) **Result:** more varied, stronger stacks (e.g., ~3 Ancient Macemen @T100–130 vs ~11 before) and a **healthier economy**. See [KI#53.4](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#534-tremendously-improved-ai-overbuilding-very-cheap-combat-units-ancient-macemen-only-being-an-issue-as-of-now-anyways-etc-in-the-early-game-sometimes-even-at-turn-100-which-is-inefficient-and-easy-to-overshoot-if-i-may-say-but-anyways-etc-as-they-are-cheap-and-accumulate-quickly-but-are-not-too-effective-especially-as-soon-as-we-get-archer-units-anyways-etc-now-limited-especially-even-more-so-after-as-of-now-turn-50-where-they-should-be-especially-useless-much-better-military-compositions-and-better-growth-as-a-result-anyways-etc). **Update:** The cap is now **generalized beyond Ancient** using **tier-based (not era-based) thresholds** to avoid era bleed-through (e.g., Ancient Macemen don’t inherit looser Classical caps). This also aims to trim (at least in theory, data lacking to draw a conclusion on an experiment anyways etc) for example **Archers in Classical** and **Longbows/Triremes in Medieval** when they’re too cheap for their tier. In practice we see AI mixes improve (e.g., Japan AI shifting from ~75 Longbows @T200 to ~50–60 Longbows + 10–15 Camel Archers + 20–27 Samurai, run-dependent). Tunables live in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit` and [`GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml`](/Assets/XML/GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml).

